<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edmund Allenby</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1861">1861</a>–<a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Edmund Allenby, 1st Viscount Allenby</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edmund Allenby, 1st Viscount Allenby, was a British cavalry officer and field marshal. Commanding the Egyptian Expeditionary Force from 1917, he took Beersheba and Gaza and entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in December 1917, then routed the Ottoman armies at Megiddo in September 1918 and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>. From 1919 to 1925 he served as High Commissioner for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edmund-allenby.jpg" alt="Edmund Allenby" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edmund_Allenby.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
